{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function executeTransaction<T>(\n   db,\n   storeNames,\n   mode,\ncallback): Promise<T>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: packages/db/src/indexed-db-wrapper.ts:248"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Executes a callback within an IndexedDB transaction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function handles transaction lifecycle automatically:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates the transaction with the specified mode"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides the transaction and object stores to the callback"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Waits for both the callback and the transaction to complete (or abort)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the callback's result or rejects with an error"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"IndexedDB can commit while an async callback is still pending. If that callback\nlater rejects, this function rejects but cannot undo the committed writes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The return type of the callback"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"db","children":[{"type":"text","value":"db"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IDBDatabase"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The IDBDatabase instance"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"storenames","children":[{"type":"text","value":"storeNames"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A single store name or array of store names to include in the transaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mode"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IDBTransactionMode"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The transaction mode ('readonly', 'readwrite', or 'readwriteflush')"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transaction"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stores"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that performs operations within the transaction.\nReceives the transaction and a record of object stores keyed by name.\nCan be sync or async."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A promise that resolves to the callback's return value when the transaction completes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Single store\nconst result = await executeTransaction(db, 'todos', 'readwrite', (tx, stores) => {\n  stores.todos.put({ id: 1, text: 'Buy milk' })\n  return 'done'\n})\n\n// Multiple stores\nawait executeTransaction(db, ['todos', 'users'], 'readwrite', (tx, stores) => {\n  stores.todos.put({ id: 1, text: 'Task' })\n  stores.users.put({ id: 1, name: 'Alice' })\n})","lang":"typescript"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"db","text":"db","level":3},{"id":"storenames","text":"storeNames","level":3},{"id":"mode","text":"mode","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction executeTransaction<T>(\n   db,\n   storeNames,\n   mode,\ncallback): Promise<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: packages/db/src/indexed-db-wrapper.ts:248\n\nExecutes a callback within an IndexedDB transaction.\n\nThis function handles transaction lifecycle automatically:\n- Creates the transaction with the specified mode\n- Provides the transaction and object stores to the callback\n- Waits for both the callback and the transaction to complete (or abort)\n- Returns the callback's result or rejects with an error\n\nIndexedDB can commit while an async callback is still pending. If that callback\nlater rejects, this function rejects but cannot undo the committed writes.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T`\n\nThe return type of the callback\n\n## Parameters\n\n### db\n\n`IDBDatabase`\n\nThe IDBDatabase instance\n\n### storeNames\n\nA single store name or array of store names to include in the transaction\n\n`string` | `string`[]\n\n### mode\n\n`IDBTransactionMode`\n\nThe transaction mode ('readonly', 'readwrite', or 'readwriteflush')\n\n### callback\n\n(`transaction`, `stores`) => `T` \\| `Promise`\\<`T`\\>\n\nA function that performs operations within the transaction.\n                  Receives the transaction and a record of object stores keyed by name.\n                  Can be sync or async.\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`T`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves to the callback's return value when the transaction completes\n\n## Example\n\n```typescript\n// Single store\nconst result = await executeTransaction(db, 'todos', 'readwrite', (tx, stores) => {\n  stores.todos.put({ id: 1, text: 'Buy milk' })\n  return 'done'\n})\n\n// Multiple stores\nawait executeTransaction(db, ['todos', 'users'], 'readwrite', (tx, stores) => {\n  stores.todos.put({ id: 1, text: 'Task' })\n  stores.users.put({ id: 1, name: 'Alice' })\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: executeTransaction\ntitle: executeTransaction\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction executeTransaction<T>(\n   db,\n   storeNames,\n   mode,\ncallback): Promise<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: packages/db/src/indexed-db-wrapper.ts:248\n\nExecutes a callback within an IndexedDB transaction.\n\nThis function handles transaction lifecycle automatically:\n- Creates the transaction with the specified mode\n- Provides the transaction and object stores to the callback\n- Waits for both the callback and the transaction to complete (or abort)\n- Returns the callback's result or rejects with an error\n\nIndexedDB can commit while an async callback is still pending. If that callback\nlater rejects, this function rejects but cannot undo the committed writes.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T`\n\nThe return type of the callback\n\n## Parameters\n\n### db\n\n`IDBDatabase`\n\nThe IDBDatabase instance\n\n### storeNames\n\nA single store name or array of store names to include in the transaction\n\n`string` | `string`[]\n\n### mode\n\n`IDBTransactionMode`\n\nThe transaction mode ('readonly', 'readwrite', or 'readwriteflush')\n\n### callback\n\n(`transaction`, `stores`) => `T` \\| `Promise`\\<`T`\\>\n\nA function that performs operations within the transaction.\n                  Receives the transaction and a record of object stores keyed by name.\n                  Can be sync or async.\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`T`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves to the callback's return value when the transaction completes\n\n## Example\n\n```typescript\n// Single store\nconst result = await executeTransaction(db, 'todos', 'readwrite', (tx, stores) => {\n  stores.todos.put({ id: 1, text: 'Buy milk' })\n  return 'done'\n})\n\n// Multiple stores\nawait executeTransaction(db, ['todos', 'users'], 'readwrite', (tx, stores) => {\n  stores.todos.put({ id: 1, text: 'Task' })\n  stores.users.put({ id: 1, name: 'Alice' })\n})\n```\n"}
